---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Writing">
<section class="route">
  <div class="wrap section">
    <p class="kicker">Writing</p>
    <h1 data-split>Writing</h1>
    <p class="lede prose">Two subjects, and they are less separate than they look. One is how software gets built and paid for. The other is how the music business is structured, which is a long argument about distribution and rights.</p>

    <div class="case-sec" style="margin-top:36px">
      <h2 class="rv">Engineering</h2>
      <div class="dcards cols2">
        <a class="dcard spot rv" href="https://ithelp.ithome.com.tw/users/20151610/ironman/5335" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <p class="kicker" style="margin-bottom:8px">iThome Ironman 2022 &middot; 30 posts</p>
          <h3>Angular TDD from zero to one</h3>
          <p>A thirty-day series on test-driven development in Angular, working through Karma and Jasmine from the first test to a habit. Written and published daily for the full thirty days.</p>
          <p class="links-line" style="margin-top:14px"><span class="tag">Traditional Chinese</span> <span class="tag">External link</span></p>
        </a>
        <div class="dcard spot rv" aria-disabled="true" style="opacity:.72">
          <p class="kicker" style="margin-bottom:8px">In progress</p>
          <h3>Three payment rails, one entitlement</h3>
          <p>Why Course Kit resolves conflicting purchase records to the highest tier instead of the last write, and what that costs when a webhook arrives late.</p>
          <p class="links-line" style="margin-top:14px"><span class="tag">Coming soon</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="case-sec">
      <h2 class="rv">Music &amp; elsewhere</h2>
      <p class="rv prose">Originally written in Traditional Chinese while I was studying the music industry in Liverpool and working in Taipei. Translated into English for this site.</p>
      <div class="dcards cols2">
        <a class="dcard spot rv" href="/writing/music-industry-structure-and-careers">
          <h3>A Guide to Music Industry Structure and Career Paths</h3>
          <p>How the music industry is structured, the roles from A&amp;R to distribution, and the skills each one actually needs.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="dcard spot rv" href="/writing/music-copyright-royalty-streams-for-songwriters">
          <h3>Music Copyright and Royalty Streams for Songwriters</h3>
          <p>The two copyright types behind every song, how music publishers make money, and the five royalty streams songwriters and publishers split.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="dcard spot rv" href="/writing/indie-artists-overseas-tour-guide">
          <h3>How Independent Artists and Bands Can Organize an Overseas Tour</h3>
          <p>Working with booking agents, promoters and logistics when planning a tour in Western markets, and seven things worth knowing first.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="dcard spot rv" href="/writing/stop-searching-for-side-project-ideas-build-a-worklog">
          <h3>Still Looking for a Side Project Topic? You Can Stop Searching</h3>
          <p>Side projects matter, but learning notes and worklogs show your problem-solving process and technical growth just as well.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
